    "ledger": [
      {
        "id": "E1",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Introducing the llama.cpp benchmark dashboard for AMD Ryzen and Radeon",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/ggml-org/llamacpp-amd-bench",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-26T11:37:17.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-27T19:28:29.001Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E2",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "The llama.cpp × AMD Benchmark dashboard is available on Hugging Face.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/ggml-org/llamacpp-amd-bench",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-26T11:37:17.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-27T19:28:29.001Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E3",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "It lets you track prompt processing and text generation performance across llama.cpp builds, models, and quantizations, so you can explore how local inference performs on AMD Ryzen and Radeon hardware.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/ggml-org/llamacpp-amd-bench",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-26T11:37:17.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-27T19:28:29.001Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E4",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "The benchmark workflow and underlying results are public, so you can also inspect how we benchmark inference performance.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/ggml-org/llamacpp-amd-bench",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-26T11:37:17.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-27T19:28:29.001Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E5",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "The current hardware choices are Radeon 8060S (gfx1151) and Radeon AI Pro R9700S (gfx1201).",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/ggml-org/llamacpp-amd-bench",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-26T11:37:17.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-27T19:28:29.001Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "The two charts show PP512 (512 input tokens, no generation) and TG128 (128 generated tokens), both starting at context depth zero.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/ggml-org/llamacpp-amd-bench",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-26T11:37:17.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-27T19:28:29.001Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "In the Build history tab, track PP512 and TG128 across all recorded builds for the selected hardware, model, and quantization.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/ggml-org/llamacpp-amd-bench",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-26T11:37:17.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-27T19:28:29.001Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Both tests start at context depth zero ( n_depth=0 ).",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/ggml-org/llamacpp-amd-bench",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-26T11:37:17.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-27T19:28:29.001Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E9",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "PP512 measures processing 512 input tokens without generation; TG128 measures generating 128 tokens without a pre-existing context.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/ggml-org/llamacpp-amd-bench",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-26T11:37:17.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-27T19:28:29.001Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E10",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "The public gfx1151 and gfx1201 workflows are scheduled weekly and run the standard benchmarks using the llama-bench tool with Flash Attention on and off, with 10 repetitions per configuration.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/ggml-org/llamacpp-amd-bench",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-26T11:37:17.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-27T19:28:29.001Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E11",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Available GGUF formats include Q4_K_M , Q8_0 , other quantizations, and higher-precision formats such as BF16 and F16 .",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/ggml-org/llamacpp-amd-bench",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-26T11:37:17.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-27T19:28:29.001Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E12",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "llama.cpp v1.0.0 : A stronger foundation for the local AI ecosystem",
